Requirements: 5   with obligations: 5

[task-01] The reachability prefilter in `src/acceptance/defects/reachability.py`
    excludes a (defect, test) pair from judgement only when it can prove the test has no
    path to the defect. Its proof follows imports, fixtures and Python names, so it
    holds only for defects that live in Python modules.
    -> no-judgement-except-proven-unreachable  [invariant/explicit]
       The reachability prefilter excludes a (defect, test) pair from judgement only
       when it can prove the test has no path to the defect.
    -> python-module-limited-proof  [invariant/explicit]
       The reachability prefilter's proof is limited to defects that live in Python
       modules because it follows imports, fixtures, and Python names.

[task-02] When any of a defect's implicated files is not a Python module — a Markdown
    document, a config file, a data file read from disk — the prefilter makes no
    exclusion for that defect: every pair with that defect is sent to the judge. Defects
    whose implicated files are all Python modules are prefiltered by the existing rules.
    -> no-exclusion-for-non-python-implicated-files  [functional/explicit]
       When any implicated file in a defect is not a Python module, the prefilter makes
       no exclusion for that defect.
    -> all-pairs-sent-to-judge-for-defect  [functional/explicit]
       Every pair associated with the defect is sent to the judge when the defect has
       any implicated file that is not a Python module.
    -> preserve-existing-prefilter-rules-for-python-only-defects  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the existing prefiltering rules for defects whose implicated files are
       all Python modules.

[task-03] A regression test is part of the deliverable: a test that opens a non-Python
    file by path and asserts on its content, paired with a defect implicating that file,
    is judged and not prefiltered.
    -> non-python-file-content-test-judged  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test opens a non-Python file by path and asserts on its content, and a defect
       implicating that file is judged rather than prefiltered.
    -> not-prefiltered  [invariant/explicit]
       The requirement is not prefiltered.

[exclusion-01] Recognising a test that names a file's path in its source as reaching
    that file.
    -> exclude-path-name-as-reachability  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not treat a test as reaching a file solely because the test
       source names that file's path.

[exclusion-02] Any change to the judge, the defect builder or how prefiltered pairs are
    scored.
    -> no-change-to-judge-defect-builder-or-scoring  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter the judge, the defect builder, or how prefiltered pairs
       are scored.

